within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.L_AntineoplasticAndImmunomodulatingAgents.L01F_MonoclonalAntibodiesAndAntibodyDrugConjugates.L01FC02_Isatuximab;
model Isatuximab "Isatuximab — default model: Isatuximab_Fau2020_reference"
  extends Isatuximab_Fau2020_reference;
  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>The default model of isatuximab: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.L_AntineoplasticAndImmunomodulatingAgents.L01F_MonoclonalAntibodiesAndAntibodyDrugConjugates.L01FC02_Isatuximab.Isatuximab_Fau2020_reference\">Isatuximab_Fau2020_reference</a>, chosen among the models extracted from papers (reviewer verdict, ground-truth agreement, completeness). All models of isatuximab in this package:</p><ul><li><code>Isatuximab_Fau2020_reference</code></li><li><code>Isatuximab_Koiwai2021_PD_m_protein</code></li><li><code>Isatuximab_Koiwai2021_PD_m_protein_2</code></li><li><code>Isatuximab_Koiwai2021_PD_m_protein_3</code></li></ul><h4>About isatuximab</h4><p>Isatuximab is a monoclonal antibody that inhibits CD38 and is used to treat multiple myeloma. It is authorised in the European Union and is used in cancer treatment.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q20707906\">Wikidata Q20707906</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Isatuximab\">Isatuximab</a>.</p></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from default: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: default</li></ul></body></html>"), experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 7257600, Tolerance = 1e-9, Interval = 1));
end Isatuximab;
